## Install

>[!NOTE]
>PRTGN_Wav uses Rodio to play sound. Rodio used the `cpal` library to send audio to the OS. 'ALSA' development files are needed to build 'cpal' on Linux. These are provided as part of the 'libasound2-dev' package on Debian and Ubuntu distributions and 'alsa-lib-devel' on Fedora.

### Debian Based Linux (Ubuntu variations, Raspberry Pi OS, Debian (obviously), e.t.c.)

1. Download and install the Debian Package (.deb) file. Make sure you have the right prossesor type. (x86_64 or Aarm64)

### Feadora / RHEL Based Linux (Fedora, Red Hat Enterprise Linux (RHEL), Rocky Linux, Cent OS, e.t.c.)

1. Download and install the RPM Package Manager/Red Hat Package Manager (.rpm) file. Make sure you have the right prossesor type. (x86_64 or Aarm64)

### Microsoft Windows (Built for 11 but should work elsewhere)

1. Download and install the Windows Executable (.exe) file. Make sure you have the right prossesor type. (x86_64 or Aarm64)

